const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文研究当同时检验大量基金时，如何区分由估计运气产生的显著alpha、技能、零alpha与非技能表现。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The article asks how to separate apparent mutual-fund alpha caused by estimation luck from skill, zero-alpha performance, and unskilled performance when many funds are tested together. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它在允许基金alpha估计之间存在依赖的前提下应用错误发现控制，因此基金全集、基准模型和存续处理是核心。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It applies false-discovery control to a broad fund sample while allowing dependence across estimated alphas, so the fund universe, benchmark model, and survival treatment are central. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要毛和净基金收益、费用、因子收益、基金标识、进入退出日期、份额类别处理、基准设定和完整的已清盘基金历史。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"Inputs include gross and net fund returns, expenses, factor returns, fund identifiers, entry and exit dates, share-class treatment, benchmark specification, and a historically complete dead-fund record. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"该方法改变了多基金样本中显著alpha的解释方式，并不在没有复现完整设计时识别某只在售基金经理为有技能。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The method changes how significant alphas are interpreted in a multiple-fund population; it does not identify a particular live manager as skilled without reproducing the full design. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"纳入关闭和合并基金；声明费用处理和基准因子；保留设立与清盘日期；定义检验家族；将估计与后续验证分开。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Include closed and merged funds; declare fee treatment and benchmark factors; preserve fund inception and liquidation dates; specify the testing family; and separate estimation from later validation. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance · DOI record。历史基金分类既不是产品推荐也不是未来表现预测，遗漏已清盘基金会实质改变推断。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance · DOI record. Historical fund classifications are neither product recommendations nor forward performance forecasts, and omitting dead funds can materially alter the inference. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2009.01527.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“False Discoveries in Mutual Fund Performance: Measuring Luck in Estimated Alphas”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史基金分类既不是产品推荐也不是未来表现预测，遗漏已清盘基金会实质改变推断。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “False Discoveries in Mutual Fund Performance: Measuring Luck in Estimated Alphas”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
